WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.030
Hank: Good morning, John.

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:04.350
John: Good morning, Hank, actually, that was
too low energy, let's have them do it.

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:07.009
Crowd: Good morning, John, it's Friday!

00:00:07.009 --> 00:00:11.420
Hank: John, I want to let you know that it
is possible to clean your lens.

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:14.690
John: Oh, oh no, that's not something that
I do, that's just not part of my aesthetic,

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:15.690
but go on.

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:17.730
Hank: We are currently on the Mainstage of
VidCon 2015.

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:18.730
John: Lot of people here.

00:00:18.730 --> 00:00:21.840
Hank: It kind of surprises me that we've only
been doing this for eight years.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:25.470
John: Yeah, I mean, eight years is a lot of
time by some measures, right?

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:29.779
Obviously, it's most of YouTube ten-year history,
but it's also a very short amount of time,

00:00:29.779 --> 00:00:31.860
like, it's only 2 presidential terms.

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:35.300
Hank: A baby in eight years only becomes an
eight year old.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:38.960
And an eight year old is basically just like
a big baby.

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:40.969
John: Mmm, strongly, strongly disagree.

00:00:40.969 --> 00:00:44.070
I would say that an eight year old is a--just
a smaller adult.

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:47.350
Hank: Are there any eight year olds here?

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:48.350
John: Wow, there is!

00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:54.739
Hank, there are people at VidCon who are younger
than the first vlogbrothers video, and now,

00:00:54.739 --> 00:00:58.149
I have become aware of how old I am.

00:00:58.149 --> 00:01:02.079
So there have been many important cultural
institutions that have come out of online

00:01:02.079 --> 00:01:03.790
video in the last eight years.

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:10.540
Gangnam style, Justin Bieber, the double rainbow
guy, and of course, the ice bucket challenge

00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:14.203
featuring Bill Gates, I don't know if Bill
Gates is here tonight, Bill?

00:01:14.203 --> 00:01:16.850
Here's probably in Tanzania doing something
about poverty.

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:17.850
We love you, Bill!

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:21.040
We wish you were here, but you have other
work, it's important.

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:24.990
Can I just interrupt you to say that your
glasses are so dirty that you have no right

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:26.190
to make fun of my lens?

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:30.549
Hank: So we started VidCon in 2010 in the
basement of a hotel in Los Angeles in Century

00:01:30.549 --> 00:01:31.549
City.

00:01:31.549 --> 00:01:35.630
It is somewhat bigger than that now, but we
had a lot of people then and here are some

00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:36.650
of them, this is the first VidCon.

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:37.650
John: The first VidCon.

00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:38.650
Hank: From VidCon 2010.

00:01:38.650 --> 00:01:44.060
John: Tyler Oakley, Rhett and Link, Dave Days,
Shay Carl is there, iJustine is there, many

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:47.710
of these people are still at VidCon this year,
and for many of them, their lives have changed

00:01:47.710 --> 00:01:48.710
dramatically.

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:49.710
Smosh has gone on to like, make movies.

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:53.649
Hank: They've got a movie coming out this
week, and Kian's movie came out this week.

00:01:53.649 --> 00:01:56.030
And your movie came out this week.

00:01:56.030 --> 00:01:57.780
John: That is true, yes, go see Paper Towns.

00:01:57.780 --> 00:01:58.780
Hank: How are you feeling about it?

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:03.060
John: Uh, incredibly anxious, I've been feeling
a little bit like maybe, maybe, maybe they

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:06.759
shouldn't have scheduled VidCon and the movie
on the same day.

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:08.539
Maybe I should retape that.

00:02:08.539 --> 00:02:12.670
So when we started VidCon in 2010, we knew
that YouTube was a big deal, but we had no

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:15.750
idea, like, how big of a deal it was going
to become.

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:20.790
Hank: Right, like, uh, we did not know that
we were taking power away from giant corporations

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:23.170
that made content, and they didn't either.

00:02:23.170 --> 00:02:24.570
John: Yeah, but uh--

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:27.150
Hank: They've realized it now, and they're
here, and they're being very nice to us.

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:31.230
John: Yeah, so thank you, giant corporations,
for your presence making everything so fancy.

00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:35.970
Stay on YouTube, but be cool about it, that's
all we ask.

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:39.590
Hank: I'm very--I'm proud of VidCon.

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:40.590
Shh.

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:42.849
John: Hey guys, we're trying to vlog here!

00:02:42.849 --> 00:02:48.250
Hank: I'm very proud of VidCon, but I'm mostly
proud to be some small part of this giant

00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:53.910
weird cultural explosion that has taken the
power and put it into the hands of the people

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:57.590
that it should be in, which is the people
who watch the content and the people who make

00:02:57.590 --> 00:03:00.720
it, and that's--that's the beauty of VidCon
for me.

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:05.519
John: For those of you inside of the camera,
thank you for paying attention and for being

00:03:05.519 --> 00:03:07.370
parts of these communities.

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:11.820
Thank you, and don't forget to be awesome,
and Hank, I will see you on Tuesday.

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:13.430
Hank: It's my video, so...John...

00:03:13.430 --> 00:03:15.850
John: And John, I will see you on Friday.

00:03:15.850 --> 00:03:16.850
Hank: No.

00:03:16.850 --> 00:03:17.850
John: You say that.

00:03:17.850 --> 00:03:18.850
That's your line.

00:03:18.850 --> 00:03:19.850
Hank: Yeah.

00:03:19.850 --> 00:03:20.850
John, very well said, and I will see you on
Friday.

00:03:20.850 --> 00:03:21.569
John: Really good work, Hank.

